From: Goldwyn Rodrigues <rgoldwyn@suse.com>
Subject: netfs: Fix potential UAF in netfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pages()
Patch-mainline: never, kABI fix
References: CVE-2026-64216 bsc#1272802

patch patches.suse/netfs-Fix-potential-UAF-in-netfs_unlock_abandoned_read_pag.patch changed
struct netfs_io_request to use folio *no_unlock_folio instead of pgoff_t no_unlock_folio.
The no_unlock_folio is modified by netfs only, even though struct netfs_io_request is
accessed by cifs or afs, so it should be safe to change.

The patch does not change the size of struct netfs_io_request.

Signed-off-by: Goldwyn Rodrigues <rgoldwyn@suse.com>
Reviewed-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>

---
 include/linux/netfs.h |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/include/linux/netfs.h
+++ b/include/linux/netfs.h
@@ -268,7 +268,11 @@ struct netfs_io_request {
 	atomic64_t		issued_to;	/* Write issuer folio cursor */
 	unsigned long long	collected_to;	/* Point we've collected to */
 	unsigned long long	cleaned_to;	/* Position we've cleaned folios to */
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
 	const struct folio	*no_unlock_folio; /* Don't unlock this folio after read */
+#else
+	pgoff_t			no_unlock_folio;
+#endif
 	size_t			prev_donated;	/* Fallback for subreq->prev_donated */
 	refcount_t		ref;
 	unsigned long		flags;
